    "public_api_change": "ADDITIVE",
    "schema_diff_summary": "cache.rs has one test module named tests. Add the new test function at the end of that module, before its closing brace. Do not write a second mod tests. Replace the inner function byte inside theme_bits with channel_byte at module scope. The body is one expression: (channel.clamp(0.0, 1.0) * 255.0).round() as u32. Do not add an if for a non-finite channel. Do not nest an if inside an if. theme_bits stays pub(crate). theme_bits calls channel_byte for alpha, red, green, and blue. Keep the shifts: alpha at 24, red at 16, green at 8, and blue at 0. Do not touch KeyedCache, get, insert, or clear. The existing test theme_bits_change_when_one_channel_changes stays green. Do not rewrite its assertions. The test a_non_finite_channel_is_zero checks channel_byte of 1.0 is 255. channel_byte of 0.0 is 0. channel_byte of 2.0 is 255. channel_byte of f32::NAN is 0. Branch from the current tip of main. base_sha records that tip at planning time. If main has moved, use the new tip. Keep the change under about 60 lines. Run the full test module named in the commands, not only the new test."
  },
